-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Board shall have as members \nthe following:\n(1) The Secretary of Commerce, who \nshall be the chairman of the Board.\n(2) The Secretary of Defense.\n(3) The Postmaster General.\n(4) The Secretary of Health, Educa­\ntion, and Welfare.\n(5) The Chairman of the Interstate \nCommerce Commission.\n(6) The Administrator of General \nServices.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Each head of agency referred to \nin subsection (b) may provide for an \nalternate member who shall serve as a \nmember of the Board in lieu of the regu­\nlar member representing the agency \nwhen such regular member is unable to \nattend any meeting of the Board; and \nany alternate member shall while serving \nas such have in all respects the same \nstatus as a member of the Board as would \nthe regular member in whose place he is \nserving.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) Three members of the Board shall \nconstitute a quorum thereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 1(d)","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec1(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. The functions and duties of \nthe Board shall be as follows:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) To provide leadership to, and to \ncoordinate the traffic safety aspects of \nprograms carried on by, the departments \nand agencies of the Federal Government.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) To evaluate the continuing needs \nin traffic safety research and to formu­\nlate plans, priorities, and programs for \nthe conduct of or for assistance to the \nmost urgently needed research through \ndepartments and agencies of the Federal \nGovernment.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) To consult and cooperate with \nState and local officials having a public \nresponsibility for traffic safety and their \nnational associations, with the motor\nvehicle industry, and with other related \ninterests, in the development and im­\nprovement, and particularly in the ap­\nplication, of traffic safety standards in \nareas such as uniform traffic laws, en­\nforcement practices, accident records, \ndriver licensing, motor vehicle equip­\nment and inspection, traffic engineer­\ning, and safety education.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) To conduct continuing studies of \nnational traffic safety needs as they re­\nlate to legislative and administrative ac­\ntions by the Federal Government, and \nto report thereon.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 2(d)","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec2(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) To perform such other functions \nand duties as the President may direct \nto coordinate more effectively the pol­\nicies, programs, and functions of the \ndepartments and agencies of the Fed­\neral Government relating to traffic \nsafety, including accident reporting, and \nto insure an orderly relationship among \nFederal, State, and local traffic safety \nprograms.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 2(e)","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec2(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Consonant with law, each \nagency represented on the Board shall, \nas n^ay be necessary for the effectuation \nof the purpose of this order, furnish as­\nsistance to the Board in accordance with \nsection 214 of the act of May 3, 1945, 59 \nStat. 134 (31 U.S.C. 691). Such assist­\nance may include detailing employees to \nthe Board, one of whom may serve as \nExecutive Officer, to perform such func­\ntions, consistent with the purpose of \nthis order, as the Board may assign to \nthem.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 3","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. The Board shall be advisory to \nits individual members and to other \nheads of executive agencies; and this \norder shall not be construed as sub­\njecting any agency, officer, or function \nto its control. The President’s Com­\nmittee for Traffic Safety (provided for in \nExecutive Order No. 10858 of January \n13, 1960) shall serve as consultant and \nadvisor to the Board.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 4","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 5. The Board shall, from time \nto time, submit reports to the President \non the national progress in traffic safety. \nThe first such report shall include de­\nterminations of the status of Federal \nlegislative and administrative needs in \nthe several areas of traffic safety and \nrecommendations for executive or legis­\nlative action.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3; Sec. 5","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10898#sec5","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"25 FR 12429, PDF pages 3-3","sha256":"365c4831298d98c96235b0d637c2e1a842ec456a011cd199c71b78e3a5996b5f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1960-12-06/pdf/FR-1960-12-06.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 13 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:10898"}
